IMPORT prelude

-- Work Injury Compensation Act 2019 (Singapore) -- how much compensation I am owed.
--
-- SEAT: the employee injured at work (for death compensation, the employee whose death it is: the question is asked
-- on that employee's behalf).
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 4(5) (partial and total incapacity), s 14 and First Schedule paragraphs 1 (death), 2 (total
-- incapacity, C + 0.25C), 3(1) (partial incapacity) and 4(1), 4(4) and 4(5)(d) (temporary incapacity, as a rate per day),
-- s 16(1) and First Schedule paragraph 5(1) (medical treatment), with Tables A and B as data.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 1 December 2025, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/WICA2019.txt. TABLES A AND B are taken from
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/WICA2019.first-schedule-tables.txt, deposited beside it because the main text loses a
-- row at each page break of both tables (see NOTES.md).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the computation of AME (average monthly earnings, First Schedule paragraph 6, with several Commissioner
-- discretions) -- AME is an input; the Fourth Schedule's percentages (the percentage of loss of earning capacity is an
-- input); paragraph 3(2) (aggregation); paragraph 4(2), (3) and the rest of 4(5); how a monthly AME becomes a daily
-- payment (the Act says payments are "based on" AME and fixes no divisor); s 15 (medical reports); s 16(2) to (8);
-- s 17 (the payment interval, review and commutation); the Fifth Schedule (platform workers).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the injured employee, with the design
-- defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. It is not
-- for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Work Injury Compensation Act 2019 -- the amount of compensation, from the employee's seat`

§§ `First Schedule Tables A and B -- the multiplying factors`

-- Paragraph 1(1): the factor in Table A is chosen "according to the age on the next birthday of the deceased employee
-- at the time of the accident"; paragraph 2(a) chooses from Table B the same way. Not the age at death, not the age
-- at the claim. Both tables run from "14 and below" to "66 and above", 53 rows.
DECLARE `factor row` HAS
    `age on next birthday` IS A NUMBER
    `Table A factor`       IS A NUMBER
    `Table B factor`       IS A NUMBER

`Tables A and B` MEANS
    --                    age,   A,   B
    LIST (`factor row` OF 14, 136, 181)  -- "14 and below"
       , (`factor row` OF 15, 135, 180)
       , (`factor row` OF 16, 135, 179)
       , (`factor row` OF 17, 134, 178)
       , (`factor row` OF 18, 134, 178)
       , (`factor row` OF 19, 133, 177)
       , (`factor row` OF 20, 132, 176)
       , (`factor row` OF 21, 132, 175)
       , (`factor row` OF 22, 131, 174)
       , (`factor row` OF 23, 130, 173)
       , (`factor row` OF 24, 129, 172)
       , (`factor row` OF 25, 128, 170)
       , (`factor row` OF 26, 127, 169)
       , (`factor row` OF 27, 127, 168)
       , (`factor row` OF 28, 125, 167)
       , (`factor row` OF 29, 124, 165)
       , (`factor row` OF 30, 123, 164)
       , (`factor row` OF 31, 122, 162)
       , (`factor row` OF 32, 121, 160)
       , (`factor row` OF 33, 120, 159)
       , (`factor row` OF 34, 118, 157)
       , (`factor row` OF 35, 117, 155)
       , (`factor row` OF 36, 115, 153)
       , (`factor row` OF 37, 114, 151)
       , (`factor row` OF 38, 112, 149)
       , (`factor row` OF 39, 110, 146)
       , (`factor row` OF 40, 108, 144)
       , (`factor row` OF 41, 107, 142)
       , (`factor row` OF 42, 106, 140)
       , (`factor row` OF 43, 105, 138)
       , (`factor row` OF 44, 104, 136)
       , (`factor row` OF 45, 103, 134)
       , (`factor row` OF 46, 102, 132)
       , (`factor row` OF 47, 101, 130)
       , (`factor row` OF 48, 100, 128)
       , (`factor row` OF 49,  98, 126)
       , (`factor row` OF 50,  96, 124)
       , (`factor row` OF 51,  94, 122)
       , (`factor row` OF 52,  92, 120)
       , (`factor row` OF 53,  90, 118)
       , (`factor row` OF 54,  88, 116)
       , (`factor row` OF 55,  86, 114)
       , (`factor row` OF 56,  84, 111)
       , (`factor row` OF 57,  82, 108)
       , (`factor row` OF 58,  80, 105)
       , (`factor row` OF 59,  78, 102)
       , (`factor row` OF 60,  75,  99)
       , (`factor row` OF 61,  72,  96)
       , (`factor row` OF 62,  68,  92)
       , (`factor row` OF 63,  63,  87)
       , (`factor row` OF 64,  58,  82)
       , (`factor row` OF 65,  53,  77)
       , (`factor row` OF 66,  48,  72)  -- "66 and above"

-- "14 and below" and "66 and above" are the end rows; every other age has its own row.
-- An age on a next birthday is a whole number. A fractional age matches no row, and the lookup then answers NOTHING:
-- that is the encoding saying it cannot answer, not a figure of zero.
GIVEN `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `factor row`
DECIDE `the row of Tables A and B for` `the age` IS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `age on next birthday` EQUALS `the band`) `Tables A and B`
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST r
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the band` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the age` AT MOST 14 THEN 14
                IF `the age` AT LEAST 66 THEN 66
                OTHERWISE `the age`

GIVEN `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my Table A factor` IS
    CONSIDER `the row of Tables A and B for` `the age`
    WHEN JUST r THEN JUST (r's `Table A factor`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my Table B factor` IS
    CONSIDER `the row of Tables A and B for` `the age`
    WHEN JUST r THEN JUST (r's `Table B factor`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§ `The facts of my injury`

DECLARE `My injury` HAS
    -- "AME": average monthly earnings, computed under First Schedule paragraph 6. Not encoded; I state it.
    `my AME`                                                   IS A NUMBER
    `my age on my next birthday at the time of the accident`   IS A NUMBER
    -- Paragraphs 1(2), 1(3), 2(b), 2(c), 5(1)(b): the figures differ for an accident "before" and "on or after"
    -- 1 November 2025 (S 694/2025). The date of the accident decides, not the date of the claim.
    `my accident happened on or after 1 November 2025`         IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 4(5), paragraph 3(1): "the aggregate percentage of the loss of earning capacity", from the Fourth Schedule
    -- or, for an injury not listed there, assessed. In percent: 100 is 100%.
    `my percentage of loss of earning capacity`                IS A NUMBER

-- The clamp the Schedule applies with different numbers each time: "if the amount obtained ... is less than $X -- $X;
-- or ... if ... more than $Y -- $Y". "Less than" and "more than", so each bound is itself payable.
GIVEN `the amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the floor`  IS A NUMBER
      `the cap`    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the amount held between the floor and the cap` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the amount` LESS THAN `the floor`  THEN `the floor`
        IF `the amount` GREATER THAN `the cap` THEN `the cap`
        OTHERWISE `the amount`

§§ `4(5) -- is my incapacity partial or total`

-- s 4(5): where I have permanent or current incapacity, I have "(a) partial incapacity ... if -- (i) the incapacity
-- reduces the individual's earning capacity in every work that the individual was capable of undertaking at the time
-- of the accident ...; and (ii) the aggregate percentage of the loss of earning capacity ... is less than 100%; or
-- (b) total incapacity if -- (i) the incapacity incapacitates the individual for any work ...; and (ii) the aggregate
-- percentage ... is 100% or more."
-- Limb (i) of each is taken to go with the percentage (an inference: an assessment of 100% is read as incapacitating
-- me for any work). A percentage of 0 is no loss of earning capacity, so neither limb is met.
DECLARE `Kind of incapacity` IS ONE OF
    `total incapacity`
    `partial incapacity`
    `no loss of earning capacity`

GIVEN `the injury` IS A `My injury`
GIVETH A `Kind of incapacity`
DECIDE `Is my permanent or current incapacity partial or total` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the injury`'s `my percentage of loss of earning capacity` AT LEAST 100 THEN `total incapacity`
        IF `the injury`'s `my percentage of loss of earning capacity` GREATER THAN 0 THEN `partial incapacity`
        OTHERWISE `no loss of earning capacity`

§§ `First Schedule paragraph 1 -- death`

-- Para 1(1): "where death results from a work injury, the amount of compensation payable must be paid in a lump sum,
-- obtained by multiplying the AME of the deceased employee by the appropriate factor in the second column of Table A".
-- Para 1(2): accident before 1 November 2025 -- less than $76,000 is raised to $76,000, more than $225,000 cut to
-- $225,000. Para 1(3): on or after -- $91,000 and $269,000.
GIVEN `the injury` IS A `My injury`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What lump sum is payable for my death` IS
    CONSIDER `What is my Table A factor` (`the injury`'s `my age on my next birthday at the time of the accident`)
    WHEN JUST factor THEN
        JUST (`the amount held between the floor and the cap` (`the injury`'s `my AME` TIMES factor)
                   (IF `the injury`'s `my accident happened on or after 1 November 2025` THEN 91000 ELSE 76000)
                   (IF `the injury`'s `my accident happened on or after 1 November 2025` THEN 269000 ELSE 225000))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§ `First Schedule paragraph 2 -- total incapacity`

-- Para 2: "the amount of compensation calculated in accordance with the formula C + 0.25C must be paid in a lump sum,
-- where C is -- (a) ... an amount obtained by multiplying the AME of the employee by the appropriate factor in ...
-- Table B ...; (b) where the accident takes place before 1 November 2025 -- (i) ... less than $97,000 -- $97,000; or
-- (ii) ... more than $289,000 -- $289,000; and (c) where the accident takes place on or after 1 November 2025 --
-- (i) ... less than $116,000 -- $116,000; or (ii) ... more than $346,000 -- $346,000."
--
-- THE FLOOR AND CAP BITE ON C, before the quarter is added. So the most payable for total incapacity is 1.25 times
-- the cap: $432,500 on or after 1 November 2025, $361,250 before.
GIVEN `the injury` IS A `My injury`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my C` IS
    CONSIDER `What is my Table B factor` (`the injury`'s `my age on my next birthday at the time of the accident`)
    WHEN JUST factor THEN
        JUST (`the amount held between the floor and the cap` (`the injury`'s `my AME` TIMES factor)
                   (IF `the injury`'s `my accident happened on or after 1 November 2025` THEN 116000 ELSE 97000)
                   (IF `the injury`'s `my accident happened on or after 1 November 2025` THEN 346000 ELSE 289000))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§ `First Schedule paragraph 3(1) -- partial incapacity`

-- Para 3(1): "(a) in the case of an injury specified in the Fourth Schedule -- by multiplying C (mentioned in
-- paragraph 2) by the percentage of loss of earning capacity caused by the injury as specified in that Schedule; and
-- (b) in the case of an injury not specified in the Fourth Schedule -- by multiplying C ... by the percentage of loss
-- of earning capacity caused by the injury (assuming that it is permanent) in every employment which the employee
-- was capable of undertaking". Both limbs do the same arithmetic; they differ only in where the percentage comes from.
--
-- One question for both paragraphs, since s 4(5) decides which applies: 100% or more is TOTAL incapacity under
-- paragraph 2, never "partial incapacity at 100%" under paragraph 3.
GIVEN `the injury` IS A `My injury`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What lump sum am I owed for my permanent or current incapacity` IS
    CONSIDER `What is my C` `the injury`
    WHEN JUST c THEN
        CONSIDER `Is my permanent or current incapacity partial or total` `the injury`
        WHEN `total incapacity`   THEN JUST (c PLUS 0.25 TIMES c)
        WHEN `partial incapacity` THEN JUST (c TIMES `the injury`'s `my percentage of loss of earning capacity` DIVIDED BY 100)
        WHEN `no loss of earning capacity` THEN JUST 0
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§ `First Schedule paragraph 4 -- temporary incapacity, day by day`

-- Para 4(1): for "each day within a period of one year starting on the date of the accident ... that the employee is
-- on hospitalisation leave, medical leave or light duties granted due to the work injury", periodical payments
-- "based on any one of the following amounts":
--   (a) "for the first 60 days of hospitalisation leave -- the employee's AME";
--   (b) "for any subsequent days of hospitalisation leave -- two-thirds of the employee's AME";
--   (c) "for the first 14 days of medical leave and light duties -- (i) when ... on medical leave -- the employee's AME;
--       and (ii) when ... on light duties -- the shortfall (if any) in the employee's actual wages for that period
--       below the employee's AME";
--   (d) "for any subsequent days of medical leave or light duties" -- two-thirds of AME, or the shortfall below
--       two-thirds of AME.
-- Para 4(4): certified by a health professional of an approved medical institution "to be ill enough to need to be
-- hospitalised but ... not hospitalised for any reason whatsoever, the employee is deemed to be hospitalised."
-- Para 4(5)(d): not on leave or light duties on "(i) any day when the employee takes a rest day or paid leave under
-- the Employment Act 1968 or the Child Development Co-Savings Act 2001".
--
-- READING. "The first 14 days of medical leave and light duties" is read as ONE count shared by both kinds of day.
-- The other reading, 14 of each, is open on the words. The answer is a RATE, not a sum: the Act fixes no way of
-- turning a monthly AME into a daily payment.
DECLARE `Kind of day` IS ONE OF `hospitalisation leave`, `medical leave`, `light duties`

DECLARE `Rate for the day` IS ONE OF
    `my AME rate`
    `two-thirds of my AME rate`
    `the shortfall of my actual wages below my AME`
    `the shortfall of my actual wages below two-thirds of my AME`
    `nothing for this day`

DECLARE `My day off work` HAS
    `the kind of day`                                                               IS A `Kind of day`
    `I was certified by an approved medical institution as needing hospitalisation but was not hospitalised` IS A BOOLEAN
    `which day of hospitalisation leave this is`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `which day of medical leave and light duties, counted together, this is`        IS A NUMBER
    `the day falls within one year starting on the date of my accident`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am taking a rest day or paid leave under the Employment Act 1968 or the Child Development Co-Savings Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the day` IS A `My day off work`
GIVETH A `Rate for the day`
DECIDE `What am I paid for this day off work` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the day`'s `the day falls within one year starting on the date of my accident` THEN `nothing for this day`
        IF `the day`'s `I am taking a rest day or paid leave under the Employment Act 1968 or the Child Development Co-Savings Act 2001` THEN `nothing for this day`
        IF     `the day`'s `the kind of day` EQUALS `hospitalisation leave`
            OR `the day`'s `I was certified by an approved medical institution as needing hospitalisation but was not hospitalised`
          THEN IF   `the day`'s `which day of hospitalisation leave this is` AT MOST 60
               THEN `my AME rate`
               ELSE `two-thirds of my AME rate`
        IF `the day`'s `the kind of day` EQUALS `medical leave`
          THEN IF   `the day`'s `which day of medical leave and light duties, counted together, this is` AT MOST 14
               THEN `my AME rate`
               ELSE `two-thirds of my AME rate`
        OTHERWISE
               IF   `the day`'s `which day of medical leave and light duties, counted together, this is` AT MOST 14
               THEN `the shortfall of my actual wages below my AME`
               ELSE `the shortfall of my actual wages below two-thirds of my AME`

§§ `16(1) and First Schedule paragraph 5 -- my medical treatment`

-- s 16(1): the employer "is liable to pay compensation in accordance with paragraph 5 of the First Schedule for the
-- following medical treatment received by an employee for a work injury: (a) medical treatment -- (i) by a health
-- professional or at an approved medical institution; and (ii) that is certified by any attending health professional
-- to be necessary; (b) where the employee is an employee mentioned in section 9, medical treatment by a health
-- professional -- (i) received outside Singapore for a work injury sustained in an accident that occurs outside
-- Singapore; and (ii) that, in the opinion of the Commissioner, is required immediately due to the nature of the work
-- injury". The Commissioner's opinion is an input.
-- Para 5(1): the compensation "is the lower of the following amounts: (a) the cost of medical treatment received by the
-- employee within a period of one year after the date of the accident causing the injury; (b) the following amount per
-- accident per employee: (i) ... before 1 November 2025 -- $45,000; (ii) ... on or after 1 November 2025 -- $53,000."
DECLARE `My medical treatment` HAS
    `treated by a health professional or at an approved medical institution, and certified necessary by an attending health professional` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am an employee mentioned in section 9, treated abroad by a health professional for an accident abroad` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner is of the opinion the treatment abroad was required immediately` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the cost of treatment I received within one year after the accident`           IS A NUMBER
    `the cost of treatment I received after that year`                              IS A NUMBER
    `my accident happened on or after 1 November 2025`                              IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the treatment` IS A `My medical treatment`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my medical treatment must my employer pay` IS
    IF      `the treatment`'s `treated by a health professional or at an approved medical institution, and certified necessary by an attending health professional`
        OR  (    `the treatment`'s `I am an employee mentioned in section 9, treated abroad by a health professional for an accident abroad`
             AND `the treatment`'s `the Commissioner is of the opinion the treatment abroad was required immediately`)
    THEN `the lower of` (`the treatment`'s `the cost of treatment I received within one year after the accident`)
                        (IF `the treatment`'s `my accident happened on or after 1 November 2025` THEN 53000 ELSE 45000)
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
        `the lower of` x y MEANS IF x LESS THAN y THEN x ELSE y
